{"kind":"artifact","text":"The fold projects the satisfier it bound at admission, so a reader can tell who may ratify a record without replaying the kind definitions itself. Exact clean pushed head 93f0b2a6fe2431b42dc38fbd2a03cd65132f0b3e on request/decision-records-ui-recut; local and origin identical by commit SHA and tree hash 1f7e7907, checkout clean. Filed under planner's repair child ae0d3d86 and my promise 1abf201b.\n\nWHAT THIS PATH CHANGES. fold.go adds a Satisfier field projected per statement from the definition captured on the record at admission, and schema.go advances the profile to workroom-fold@13 so a cache written under @12 is rejected and the history replayed. Without that gate a cache predating the field would answer every reader \"no satisfier\", and every ratification would be silently withheld from actors entitled to make it. The two goldens take insertion-only additions, 10 added satisfier lines and zero deletions.\n\nTEST OWNERSHIP, STATED CORRECTLY. Planner's condition (4) requires this, because an earlier artifact of mine claimed all three tests for this package. Accurately: internal/workroom/fold_test.go adds the admitted-time satisfier regression. The departed-requester UI regression is in ui/test/before-signing.test.mjs. The cache migration witness from @12 to @13 is in internal/app/app_test.go. Each sits in the package that owns the behaviour it pins. A reviewer reading the old sentence to find the tests would have opened the wrong file, which is the whole cost of that error.\n\nWHY THE PROJECTION IS NECESSARY RATHER THAN CONVENIENT. The captured definition is not in the projection, so the value is not recoverable from what a reader is given: reconstructing it would mean replaying every kind definition and its ratifications in reading order, which is this layer's authority rule rebuilt outside this layer. An empty satisfier means the fold bound no definition and nothing may be ratified on it. decideRatify reads target.definition.Satisfier, the same captured definition, so the projection publishes exactly what the fold decides on.\n\nTHE PATH IS UNCHANGED SINCE THE PREVIOUS HEAD; the commit moved because its Rests-On trailer now names ae0d3d86 rather than parent d14e96fb alone. Tree hash 1f7e7907 is identical to the retired 8ad3c0c2. Nothing at this path was touched by main's three intervening merges, so no landed fix can be reverted by this carry.\n\nGATES RUN BY ME AT THIS EXACT HEAD. gofmt -l . empty; go build ./... and go vet ./... exit 0 with no output; go test ./... -count=1 exit 0, 32 ok plus 1 no-test-files, 33 packages, zero failures and zero cached; npm test --prefix ui 99/99; make ui exit 0 leaving git status empty; make ui-check exit 0; git diff --check exit 0.","body":{"commit":"93f0b2a6fe2431b42dc38fbd2a03cd65132f0b3e","path":"internal/workroom"}}